{
  "description": "issue #688 (terminal slice): item 3 of the normative same-tick delivery list, `pending on_click events in registration order` (spec/interaction-events.md:84-89). `on_click` takes no argument, so every registered handler is a candidate for the same click: ONE click delivered at tick 1 makes both handlers pending at one drain point, and the line-1 handler prints 1 before the line-2 handler prints 2. As in the `on_key` twin, the order is pinned twice over -- by the printed values and by the handler-start `instruction` spans (the line-1 `on_click` head at seq 5 before the line-2 head at seq 8, spec/interaction-events.md:101-102) -- so a reversed drain fails on both. This also proves a single click fans out to EVERY registered handler rather than only the first or the last, which the registration-only sibling `on-click-registered-twice` (where neither handler fires) cannot show. `wait` emits its `primitive` after the pause completes (seq 11); no tick, pointer coordinate, or `turtle_id` appears in any payload -- OpenLogo v0.1 standardizes no click-coordinate reporter (spec/interaction-events.md:234-237).",
